// #1104 crash-repro fixture (v0.16 W3(c)), reduced from the Lossy conversion of
// bench/corpus/serilog/src/Serilog/Core/Sinks/Batching/BatchingSink.cs at the
// pinned submodule SHA 0597ddfb (converter options as in Calor0425CorpusLedgerTests).
//
// The C# line `_batchScheduler.MarkFailure(out var shouldDropBatch, out var shouldDropQueue);`
// converts to a hoisted `§B{~shouldDropQueue}` with NO initializer on its own line,
// followed by the call. The parser reads the next expression start as the binding's
// initializer, so the binding's value is a call whose ARGUMENT is the binding itself.
// Resolving the type of `shouldDropQueue` then types that call's arguments, which
// resolves `shouldDropQueue` again — unbounded before the fix; the host died.
//
// Reduction (each step re-crashed the unfixed tree before the next was taken):
//   1. full converted module (176 lines) → crash
//   2. keep only the enclosing class, the receiver field, and LoopAsync's
//      `§B{~shouldDropBatch}` / `§B{~shouldDropQueue}` / `§C{_batchScheduler.MarkFailure}` → crash
//   3. drop the §NS wrapper and `§B{~shouldDropBatch}` (its initializer is null,
//      it resolves in one step and is not on the cycle) → crash — this file.
// This file does NOT bind or compile — that is the point of it (the effect pass is
// reached here without a binder). It is therefore listed in
// tests/TestData/Formatting/formatter-corpus-baseline.json under
// conservativeFallbacks.semanticErrors, where the formatter records every committed
// .calr it declines to reformat because the source has semantic errors.
// The receiver field is load-bearing: a receiver that does not resolve to a type
// returns before the arguments are typed and the cycle is never entered.
§M{m001:Calor0425Leg}
  §CL{c002:BatchingSink:int:seal}
    §FLD{FailureAwareBatchScheduler:_batchScheduler:priv:readonly}

    §AMT{m018:LoopAsync:priv}
      §B{~shouldDropQueue}
      §C{_batchScheduler.MarkFailure} §A shouldDropBatch §A shouldDropQueue §/C
